Community app

NoteCraft is a community "Craft" app by Ideademic, made to fit in with the open-source Crafting
Apps of the ArtCraft team (https://getartcraft.com/), such as WordCraft, DeckCraft and GridCraft.
It is not an official ArtCraft app and is not endorsed by the ArtCraft team. It follows their
conventions and is built on their open-source shared libraries, used under their licences:
craft-libs (https://github.com/storytold/craft-libs: craft-ui, craft-i18n, craft-window,
craft-web-host, craft-pdf, MIT OR Apache-2.0) and the Craft forks of egui and winit
(https://github.com/storytold/egui, https://github.com/storytold/winit, MIT OR Apache-2.0).
Its packaging scripts and release workflows are adapted from WordCraft
(https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft) and storytold/craft-common-actions (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

NoteCraft contains no ArtCraft or Storyteller names, logos or other brand assets beyond plain-text
references like this one. If you fork it, keep it that way: don't add ArtCraft logos, and remove
any you find.

Trademarks

Microsoft, OneNote and Office are trademarks of the Microsoft group of companies. NoteCraft is an
independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by Microsoft. "OneNote"
is used only to describe the file formats NoteCraft reads and writes and the style of app it is.

Clean room

NoteCraft's .one, .onetoc2 and .onepkg support is written only from Microsoft's published Open
Specifications ([MS-ONESTORE], [MS-ONE], [MS-DTYP], [MS-OSHARED], [MS-CAB]) and observed
black-box behaviour, under the Microsoft Open Specifications Promise. No code from other OneNote
implementations, and no icons, images, templates, fonts or other assets from Microsoft products,
are used. Writing files that Microsoft OneNote opens is experimental and unverified.

